  "analysis": "This is Round 1 of a Public Goods Game. I'm agent_2 (one of 5 players). All other agents have expressed cooperative intentions and plan to contribute 15-16 tokens. Agent_1 plans 16, agent_3 plans 15, agent_4 plans 16. The game rules state: each player gets 20 tokens, contributes 0-20 to public pool, pool is multiplied by 1.6 and split equally among 5 players. My payoff = 20 - contribution + (pool × 1.6) / 5. Since all others are planning high contributions (15-16), I should match this cooperative level. If all 5 contribute 15-16, the pool would be ~75-80, multiplied by 1.6 = 120-128, divided by 5 = 24-25.6 per person. My payoff would be 20 - 15 + 24 = 29 (if contributing 15). This is better than contributing 0 which would give 20 + (60×1.6)/5 = 20 + 19.2 = 39.2 if others contribute 15. Wait, let me recalculate. If I contribute 0 and others contribute 15 each (total 60), pool = 60×1.6 = 96, split = 19.2, my payoff = 20 + 19.2 = 39.2. If I contribute 15 and others contribute 15 each (total 75), pool = 75×1.6 = 120, split = 24, my payoff = 20 - 15 + 24 = 29. So actually contributing less gives me a higher payoff if others are contributing. But this is a repeated game (20 rounds), so cooperation matters. Looking at the messages, agents are signaling high cooperation. In a one-shot game, the Nash equilibrium is to contribute 0, but in a repeated game, cooperation can be sustained. Since this is round 1 and all others are being cooperative, I should match their level. Agent_1 said 16, but I was planning 15. Let me look at what makes sense strategically. Given that agents 1, 3, and 4 are planning 15-16, and agent_0 is general, I should contribute at a similar level. I'll go with 16 to match agent_1 and agent_4, showing strong cooperation.",
  "plan": "I'll contribute 16 tokens to match the cooperative level set by agent_1 and agent_4. This sends a strong signal of cooperation and ensures a high public pool for everyone's benefit.",
  "commands": {
    "contribution": 16,
    "public_message": "I'm contributing 16 tokens to the public pool. With everyone else planning high contributions, this maximizes our collective benefit and sets a strong cooperative tone for the game."
  }
}

